00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:14.570
a scope.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:18.570
So for example I mean a standard operation,
simplest possible operation you might have

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:19.670
in a computer system is a ‘not’.

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:20.670
That's right.

00:18:20.670 --> 00:18:21.820
So how would you do a ‘not’?

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:26.401
So you prepare, you would prepare your qubit
in the zero state then you would shine a microwave

00:18:26.401 --> 00:18:32.510
a laser beam on it for a set amount of time
and it would cause the population to evolve

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:36.750
to the up state, and that's a ‘not’ gate
if it go from zero to one that's a ‘not’

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:37.750
gate.

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:41.140
If you let that light or microwave interaction
on and it would go back down to the zero state

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:44.020
and it would just keep rotating.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:47.220
So suppose I want to do something a bit more
sophisticated like an ‘and’ or something

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.470
that actually combines two qubits.

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.090
How would you how would you do that?

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:57.200
So if you had two qubits in trapped-ions,
the nice thing is that because they're charged

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:00.940
they want to repel each other, but because
there's a trapping potential on them they

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:04.640
get pushed together so they find a happy medium
where they sit.

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:07.970
But they have a shared motional mode due to
this interaction.

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:09.670
So there are a lot like a Newton's cradle.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:13.290
If you pull a ball in a Newton's cradle you
see all the balls move together.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:14.600
That’s right.

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:15.910
That’s right.

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:17.500
And so the trapped ions do the same thing.

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:22.070
If you start to shine a laser beam on one
and you excite some motion and actually excites

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:23.870
motion in in both ions.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:27.720
And so then you have a databus that you can
get the ions to talk to each other.

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:31.140
And if you had five ions you could actually
use this databus to get one in five to talk

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.140
to each other directly.

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:33.620
So you're not limited to your nearest neighbor
interactions in a trapped ion system.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:37.990
And you can use that to combine them.

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:41.920
You can use that combined motional mode to
get the qubit states to talk to each other

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:45.300
and create things like controlled ‘not’
gates, say.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:46.300
Great.

