00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:31.360
So if you if you go back to your electrical
engineering days think about the circuits

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:36.900
that you might build with resistors or capacitors
or inductors, these are varied circuit elements.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:41.610
In the case of a superconducting circuit you
actually could use an element known as a Josephson

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:42.670
junction.

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:48.200
And a Josephson junction is basically a sandwich
