00:42:22.570 --> 00:42:28.020
Yes so there's people working now on, in addition
to quantum, computing quantum networking and

00:42:28.020 --> 00:42:33.100
what you can do with quantum mechanics for
networking communication, the easiest example

00:42:33.100 --> 00:42:37.330
to explain, and it's been around for a while,
is called quantum key distribution, where

00:42:37.330 --> 00:42:42.800
you send a message between two parties say
Alice and Bob using single photons.

00:42:42.800 --> 00:42:48.690
And because the photons are encoded using
quantum mechanics you can actually make protocols

00:42:48.690 --> 00:42:50.240
that are ultra secure.

00:42:50.240 --> 00:42:57.060
And by that we mean they're tamper-proof,
meaning that even if an, an eavesdropper can't

00:42:57.060 --> 00:43:01.240
get between Alice and Bob to get the signal
because they don't have the corresponding

00:43:01.240 --> 00:43:04.320
information that was encoded in the quantum
mechanics.

00:43:04.320 --> 00:43:08.440
But even if an eavesdropper were to try and
grab the signal the protocols are tamper evident

00:43:08.440 --> 00:43:12.880
so Alice and Bob would see that immediately
when they started to talk about the results

00:43:12.880 --> 00:43:15.740
that they'd gotten and would abandon the protocol.

00:43:15.740 --> 00:43:21.660
So yes it can do things like break, break
encryption but it can also provide ultra secure

00:43:21.660 --> 00:43:22.660
protocols too.

00:43:22.660 --> 00:43:25.740
So what are you doing in your lab now to kind
of bring that into fruition?

00:43:25.740 --> 00:43:31.430
So we're working on quantum networking where
instead of sending key information, which

00:43:31.430 --> 00:43:35.350
that just sends information to generate a
key and then you would use the key for something

00:43:35.350 --> 00:43:36.350
else.

00:43:36.350 --> 00:43:39.950
We, and a lot of people in the field, are
moving towards quantum networking where you

00:43:39.950 --> 00:43:45.480
actually send quantum information directly
over some longer distance link.

00:43:45.480 --> 00:43:49.880
And so this allows you to do things like ultra
secure communication protocols or people are

00:43:49.880 --> 00:43:52.560
