over any of the qubits, you really can drive
the system to any kind of quantum quantum

01:01:17.930 --> 01:01:18.930
problem that you want.

01:01:18.930 --> 01:01:25.890
And so it's it's reprogrammable in that sense
and you can define your optimization landscape

01:01:25.890 --> 01:01:29.300
in more generality.

01:01:29.300 --> 01:01:32.700
But maybe Seth you can also comment on the
D-wave.

01:01:32.700 --> 01:01:37.010
Yeah, I mean, also let me say that you keep
on letting all of the people who possess prior

01:01:37.010 --> 01:01:40.540
knowledge into this room will make our lives
harder.

01:01:40.540 --> 01:01:42.910
So what's that about?

01:01:42.910 --> 01:01:47.869
So quantum annealer as as Jerry was saying
it's a it's actually a very old idea and classically,

01:01:47.869 --> 01:01:51.400
there's a notion called simulated annealing
classically where you want to solve a hard

01:01:51.400 --> 01:01:52.400
problem.

01:01:52.400 --> 01:01:58.550
So you want to find the the minimum value
of some function, many problems are like this,

01:01:58.550 --> 01:02:01.839
like the traveling salesman problem, I want
to find the shortest path that will get me

01:02:01.839 --> 01:02:05.430
through all the cities of the United States
and back to where I started.

01:02:05.430 --> 01:02:06.430
That's a hard problem.

01:02:06.430 --> 01:02:10.240
And so what you do is you map this problem
into finding the lowest energy state of a

01:02:10.240 --> 01:02:14.990
physical system and then you try to find this
lowest energy state by cooling, annealing,

01:02:14.990 --> 01:02:20.410
that's why it's called, annealing to get down
to this lowest energy state.

01:02:20.410 --> 01:02:23.190
Now quantum annealing is a sneaky trick that
does this quantum mechanically.

01:02:23.190 --> 01:02:25.280
You construct a quantum system.

01:02:25.280 --> 01:02:30.230
I mean for instance D-Wave quantum annealer
is a tunable device with up to a couple thousand

01:02:30.230 --> 01:02:34.869
quantum bits, and they can tune all the couplings
between them And then you set it up so that

01:02:34.869 --> 01:02:39.620
the lowest energy state encodes the answer
to your problem.and then you try to find this

01:02:39.620 --> 01:02:44.500
lowest energy state by kind of oozing in a
funky quantum mechanical state of fashion

01:02:44.500 --> 01:02:47.520
from some known state to this unknown state.

01:02:47.520 --> 01:02:50.109
And either it works or it doesn't.

01:02:50.109 --> 01:02:53.820
Now it is an interesting situation because
actually nobody knows if this works is supposed

01:02:53.820 --> 01:02:55.550
to work even in theory.

01:02:55.550 --> 01:03:00.140
And so it's one of these things where if you
build it and then you see what happens.

01:03:00.140 --> 01:03:03.800
They find that some fraction of the time they
actually get the right answer.

01:03:03.800 --> 01:03:07.200
There's a lot of argument about whether this
is happening in an intrinsically quantum mechanical

01:03:07.200 --> 01:03:09.090
way or not.

01:03:09.090 --> 01:03:12.080
But I mean these are very interesting systems
so I mean D-Wave deserves great credit for

01:03:12.080 --> 01:03:14.380
building a large scale quantum system.

01:03:14.380 --> 01:03:15.980
It's got lots of entanglement in it.

01:03:15.980 --> 01:03:20.210
It's got, you know, it's it's has thousands
of quantum bits and it's actually a beautiful

01:03:20.210 --> 01:03:21.900
system just for doing experiments on.

